UiPath-Specific Rules
Object Repository

UI selectors should be created and managed through Object Repository where applicable.

Flag as Critical if fragile inline selectors are heavily used in production UI automation and this creates confirmed runtime instability.

Flag as Warning if Object Repository is partially used but inconsistent.

If the project has no meaningful UI automation or selector files, mark this as not applicable or Manual Check.

Mail Reading

When reading mails, the process should read all unread mails.

Do not use a Top filter that may skip unread mails unless there is a documented business reason.

Flag as Critical if Top filter can cause missed production mails.

Flag as Warning if filtering strategy is unclear.

Static UI Selectors

Selectors should be robust and avoid unstable attributes where possible.

Flag as Warning if selectors depend on dynamic IDs, row indexes, temporary text, or unstable UI structure.

Coded / XAML Compatibility

When reviewing coded workflows or XAML workflows, preserve compatibility with UiPath Studio and the project package versions.

Flag as Critical if generated changes may not be supported by the current UiPath project version.

Invoke Code Try-Catch Requirement

Invoke Code activities must contain meaningful try-catch handling inside the code block when the code performs non-trivial logic, external calls, parsing, file operations, DB operations, or risky transformations.

The catch block must not swallow the exception silently.

The catch block must throw or rethrow meaningfully, preserving useful exception context.

Flag as Warning if Invoke Code contains risky logic without try-catch.

Flag as Critical if Invoke Code catches exceptions and suppresses them without throwing, logging, or returning a clear error state.

Good pattern:

Try
  risky logic
Catch ex As Exception
  Throw New Exception("Meaningful context message", ex)
End Try

Bad pattern:

Try
  risky logic
Catch
End Try
Workflow Analyzer and CLI Validation

If possible, recommend running:

uip rpa get-errors
uip rpa analyze

Do not claim analyzer errors exist unless analyzer output is available.

If analyzer/CLI cannot be run, state this under Manual Checks and keep review confidence at Medium or Low.
